  The Shape Map in powerbi/ draws context round the footpath zones, generalised and cut to the map frame:
  - suburbs and localities with the water mesh blocks cut out: Australian Bureau of Statistics, Australian Statistical
    Geography Standard (ASGS) Edition 3, Suburbs and Localities 2021 and Mesh Blocks 2021, CC BY 4.0;
  - the Yarra and other water areas cut out of the land: Vicmap Hydro, Water Area (HY_WATER_AREA_POLYGON), State of
    Victoria (Department of Transport and Planning), CC BY 4.0;
  - street outlines: City of Melbourne Open Data, Road corridors, CC BY 4.0.
  Water is not a layer: it is the map background showing where no land is drawn.

